      "next_deadline": "Homekey+ NOFA (November 26, 2024) is fully committed; the County expects 24 scattered-site beds online in FY 2026/27 and Stagecoach after rehab. Any future round would again be a County and AMI Housing joint application.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "Nevada County's Housing and Community Services Department (HCS, Tyler Barrington, Director, 950 Maidu Ave, Nevada City, 530-265-1645, Housing@nevadacountyca.gov) sits inside the Health and Human Services Agency and administers the Western Nevada County Regional Housing Trust Fund, PLHA (as delegated applicant for Grass Valley and Nevada City), state HOME and CDBG awards, the MORE mobile home program and the new Down Payment Assistance Program; the Behavioral Health and Homelessness Department (Cari Yardley, Director) holds Homekey+, BHSA and the Truckee Navigation Center; HHAP is administered by the Homeless Resource Council of the Sierras as the CoC CA-531 lead; and the Regional Housing Authority (Sutter, Nevada, Yuba, Colusa and Lake counties, Yuba City) supplies vouchers. Grass Valley, Nevada City and Truckee run their own programs (Pass 3). The County has no inclusionary ordinance, no housing impact fee and no affordable housing fee waiver program; the only land use incentive is the state density bonus ordinance. nevadacountyca.gov opens directly and the Legistar web API client 'nevco' exposes staff reports and attachments at legistar.granicus.com/nevco/attachments/. The County acts as applicant and property owner with AMI Housing as operator, so there is no open developer solicitation. Operating subsidies come from the Homekey+ operating awards and BHSA Housing Interventions; vouchers are not available (Regional Housing Authority lists closed through 2026). A developer wanting to partner should approach the Behavioral Health and Homelessness Department.",
