      "program_name": "Residential Density Bonus and Incentives for Affordable and Senior Housing (Land Use and Development Code Section 12.03.160)",
      "administering_agency": "Nevada County Community Development Agency, Planning Department",
      "funding_type": "density bonus",
      "typical_award_size": "Implements Government Code 65915 for projects of five or more units: 10% lower income, 5% very low income, 10% moderate income (for-sale), 50% senior, 50% workforce housing (60% to 150% AMI, a local category), 10% transitional foster youth, disabled veteran or homeless units, or 100% affordable projects. Bonus and incentive tables track state law (20% to 50%, up to 80% for 100% affordable within one-half mile of transit); senior developments get 20%. Parking ratios reduced per state law. Additional bonus and incentive provisions for transitional and supportive housing are in the Section governing those uses.",
